  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Li</mi><mprescripts/><none/><mn>7</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;fuses with&nbsp;a proton&nbsp;according to the nuclear reaction given below:</p>\r\r<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math></p>\r\r<p>Given that the atomic masses of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>He</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mi>Li</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>007825</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>002603</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>016004</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>931</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MeV</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, then the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>value</mi></math>&nbsp;of the reaction is</p>\r",
